    menu "Object Limits"

        config KNX_MAX_GROUP_OBJECT_PAYLOAD_BYTES
            int "Group object payload capacity (octets)"
            default 16
            range 14 254
            help
                Payload octets reserved per group object.  Each object holds two
                buffers of this size (current value plus last-transmitted value
                for send-on-change), so the cost is paid twice per object.

                The default of 16 covers every datapoint type in the catalog
                (the widest is DPT 16 at 14 octets) and keeps a group object at
                ~288 bytes instead of ~768.  Raise it only for a product that
                uses group objects as opaque transport for larger blobs.
                Oversized payloads are rejected, never truncated.
    endmenu

